(function(E){ const x = E["exam-08"] = E["exam-08"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x08-r3"] = {"id":"x08-r3","patterns":["RA-nature","GT3-history","PARA-research","PARA-cause","TR-whosevoice","TR-samewords","TR-detail","TR-paraphrase","TR-limit","TR-plural"],"title":{"en":"Reading 3: Passage 3 / Section 3","tr":"Reading 3: Passage 3 / Section 3","fa":"Reading ۳: متن ۳ (Passage 3) / بخش ۳ (Section 3)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to handle the longest passage: find details in seven sections, match opinions to five people, and complete a summary with words from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste en uzun metinle baş etmeyi öğreneceksin: yedi bölümde ayrıntı bulacak, görüşleri beş kişiyle eşleştirecek ve bir özeti metindeki kelimelerle tamamlayacaksın.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری از پس طولانی‌ترین متن بربیایی: جزئیات را در هفت بخش پیدا کنی، نظرها را با پنج نفر جور کنی و یک خلاصه را با کلمه‌های متن کامل کنی."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to choose a heading for each paragraph of a long article, complete a summary with one word from the text, and answer multiple choice questions.","tr":"Bu derste uzun bir makalenin her paragrafına bir başlık seçmeyi, bir özeti metinden tek kelimeyle tamamlamayı ve çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری برای هر پاراگراف یک مقاله‌ی بلند عنوان انتخاب کنی، یک خلاصه را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی و به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای جواب بدهی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 3: a long argument with experts","tr":"Reading Passage 3: uzmanlarla uzun bir tartışma","fa":"Reading Passage 3: بحثی طولانی با نظر متخصص‌ها"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to handle the longest passage: find details in seven sections, match opinions to five people, and complete a summary with words from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste en uzun metinle baş etmeyi öğreneceksin: yedi bölümde ayrıntı bulacak, görüşleri beş kişiyle eşleştirecek ve bir özeti metindeki kelimelerle tamamlayacaksın.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری از پس طولانی‌ترین متن بربیایی: جزئیات را در هفت بخش پیدا کنی، نظرها را با پنج نفر جور کنی و یک خلاصه را با کلمه‌های متن کامل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"14"},{"label":{"en":"Sections","tr":"Bölüm","fa":"بخش"},"value":"A-G"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: guard donkeys","tr":"Bu sınav: bekçi eşekler","fa":"این آزمون: الاغ‌های نگهبان"},"intro":{"en":"Passage 3 is the hardest: longer sentences, more opinions and more paraphrase. In this test, as often, it is about nature, here the conflict between farmers and wild animals.","tr":"Passage 3 en zor olanıdır: daha uzun cümleler, daha çok görüş ve daha çok eş anlamlı ifade. Bu sınavda, sık olduğu gibi, konu doğa; burada çiftçiler ile yaban hayvanları arasındaki çatışma.","fa":"Passage 3 سخت‌ترین است: جمله‌های بلندتر، نظرهای بیشتر و بازگویی بیشتر. در این آزمون، مثل خیلی وقت‌ها، موضوع طبیعت است؛ این‌جا کشمکش کشاورزها و حیوان‌های وحشی."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x08-r3-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-nature","PARA-research","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-nature","n":37,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 37 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 37’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۷ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Animals, farmers and wildlife","tr":"Hayvanlar, çiftçiler ve yaban hayatı","fa":"حیوان‌ها، کشاورزها و حیات وحش"},"asks":{"en":"A long passage in seven sections examines one practical solution to a conflict between farming and wild animals: why it works, the evidence, the conditions for success, the risks and the wider effects. Five people give their views.","tr":"Yedi bölümlük uzun bir metin, tarım ile yaban hayvanları arasındaki bir çatışmaya yönelik pratik bir çözümü inceliyor: neden işe yaradığı, kanıtlar, başarı koşulları, riskler ve daha geniş etkiler. Beş kişi görüşlerini söylüyor.","fa":"متنی طولانی در هفت بخش یک راه‌حل عملی را برای کشمکش بین کشاورزی و حیوان‌های وحشی بررسی می‌کند: چرا جواب می‌دهد، شواهد، شرط‌های موفقیت، خطرها و اثرهای گسترده‌تر. پنج نفر نظرشان را می‌گویند."},"fields":["The old methods","Why the idea works","The evidence","Conditions for success","Risks","Wider effects","Conclusion"],"words":[{"a":"predators","b":"foxes, coyotes, wolves / animals that kill others","tr":"yırtıcılar","fa":"شکارچی‌ها"},{"a":"traditional methods","b":"the old responses / what farmers always did","tr":"geleneksel yöntemler","fa":"روش‌های سنتی"},{"a":"instinctive","b":"natural / needs no training","tr":"içgüdüsel","fa":"غریزی"},{"a":"a fraction of the cost","b":"much cheaper","tr":"maliyetin küçük bir kısmı","fa":"کسری از هزینه"},{"a":"mixed evidence","b":"results vary / a lottery","tr":"karışık kanıtlar","fa":"شواهد ضدونقیض"},{"a":"bond with","b":"treat as its own group / companions","tr":"bağ kurmak","fa":"انس گرفتن با"},{"a":"aggressive","b":"likely to attack / injure","tr":"saldırgan","fa":"پرخاشگر"},{"a":"rich grass","b":"good pasture / lush grazing","tr":"besleyici ot","fa":"علف پربار"},{"a":"overweight","b":"obese / too fat","tr":"kilolu","fa":"اضافه‌وزن"},{"a":"scared away","b":"chased off rather than killed","tr":"korkutulup kaçırılmış","fa":"فراری داده‌شده"},{"a":"move elsewhere","b":"go to the next farm / shift the problem","tr":"başka yere gitmek","fa":"به جای دیگر رفتن"},{"a":"combined with","b":"one part of the system / alongside other methods","tr":"... ile birlikte","fa":"همراه با"}],"traps":[{"en":"\"Farmers assume X... In fact, Y.\" The statement \"many people wrongly believe X\" matches the speaker who says this, even though X is false.","tr":"\"Çiftçiler X sanıyor... Aslında Y.\" \"Birçok kişi yanlışlıkla X’e inanıyor\" ifadesi, X yanlış olsa da bunu söyleyen kişiyle eşleşir.","fa":"«کشاورزها خیال می‌کنند X... در واقع Y». جمله‌ی «خیلی‌ها به اشتباه X را باور دارند» با گوینده‌ای جور است که این را می‌گوید، حتی اگر X غلط باشد."},{"en":"Cost words appear in two sections: \"costly\" fences in A and \"a fraction of the cost\" in B. Only one compares two animals.","tr":"Maliyet kelimeleri iki bölümde geçiyor: A’da \"pahalı\" çitler, B’de \"maliyetin küçük bir kısmı\". Yalnızca biri iki hayvanı karşılaştırıyor.","fa":"کلمه‌های هزینه در دو بخش آمده‌اند: حصارهای «پرهزینه» در A و «کسری از هزینه» در B. فقط یکی دو حیوان را مقایسه می‌کند."},{"en":"In a summary, the words around the gap may come from one sentence of the passage, but the gap word may be in the next sentence. Read a little further.","tr":"Özette boşluğun etrafındaki kelimeler metnin bir cümlesinden gelebilir ama boşluk kelimesi bir sonraki cümlede olabilir. Biraz daha ileri oku.","fa":"در خلاصه، کلمه‌های دور جای خالی ممکن است از یک جمله‌ی متن باشند، اما کلمه‌ی جای خالی در جمله‌ی بعد. کمی جلوتر بخوان."}],"example":{"text":"\"Most visitors assume the fish are fed by staff. In fact, the pond provides all the food they need,\" says the keeper, Ana Silva.","item":"Who says that a common belief about the fish is wrong?","answer":"Ana Silva","why":{"en":"She reports what visitors \"assume\" and then corrects it with \"in fact\".","tr":"Ziyaretçilerin \"sandığı\" şeyi aktarıyor, sonra \"in fact\" ile düzeltiyor.","fa":"چیزی را که بازدیدکننده‌ها «خیال می‌کنند» نقل می‌کند و بعد با «in fact» اصلاحش می‌کند."}}},{"id":"RA-nature-p1","ctx":["RA-nature"],"title":{"en":"Natural history accounts","tr":"Doğa tarihi anlatıları","fa":"روایت‌های تاریخ طبیعی"},"asks":{"en":"A factual account of an animal, a plant or a natural place: how it lives, how it was discovered, why it declined and how it is protected. Statements test single facts; the notes follow the order of the text.","tr":"Bir hayvan, bitki ya da doğal bir yer hakkında bilgilendirici bir metin: nasıl yaşadığı, nasıl keşfedildiği, neden azaldığı ve nasıl korunduğu. İfadeler tek tek bilgileri sınar; notlar metnin sırasını izler.","fa":"متنی اطلاعاتی درباره‌ی یک حیوان، یک گیاه یا یک مکان طبیعی: چطور زندگی می‌کند، چطور کشف شد، چرا کم شد و چطور از آن حفاظت می‌شود. جمله‌ها اطلاعات جزئی را می‌سنجند؛ یادداشت‌ها ترتیب متن را دنبال می‌کنند."},"fields":["The species was first described in the 1800s.","Its numbers have fallen since the 1950s.","It is found only on one island.","Farmers consider it a pest.","Notes: Diet · Habitat · Threats · Protection"],"words":[{"a":"declined","b":"fell in number / became scarcer","tr":"azaldı","fa":"کم شد"},{"a":"disappeared","b":"became extinct / died out","tr":"yok oldu","fa":"از بین رفت"},{"a":"only","b":"exclusively / nowhere else","tr":"yalnızca","fa":"فقط"},{"a":"first","b":"the earliest / originally","tr":"ilk","fa":"اولین"},{"a":"increased","b":"rose / grew / expanded","tr":"arttı","fa":"افزایش یافت"},{"a":"protect","b":"conserve / save from","tr":"korumak","fa":"حفاظت کردن"},{"a":"harmful","b":"damaging / a threat to","tr":"zararlı","fa":"مضر"},{"a":"common","b":"widespread / found in many places","tr":"yaygın","fa":"رایج"},{"a":"scientists","b":"researchers / biologists","tr":"bilim insanları","fa":"دانشمندان"},{"a":"uncertain","b":"it remains unclear / not yet known","tr":"belirsiz","fa":"نامعلوم"},{"a":"caused by","b":"the result of / due to","tr":"... yüzünden","fa":"ناشی از"},{"a":"brought in","b":"introduced by humans","tr":"dışarıdan getirilmiş","fa":"وارد شده"}],"traps":[{"en":"Hedging: \"may\", \"some researchers believe\". A statement that turns this into a fact is usually FALSE or NOT GIVEN; compare carefully.","tr":"Temkinli dil: \"may\", \"bazı araştırmacılara göre\". Bunu kesin bilgiye çeviren bir ifade genelde FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN olur; dikkatle karşılaştır.","fa":"زبان محتاطانه: «may»، «بعضی پژوهشگرها معتقدند». جمله‌ای که این را به واقعیت قطعی تبدیل کند معمولاً FALSE یا NOT GIVEN است؛ دقیق مقایسه کن."},{"en":"\"Only\", \"always\", \"never\" in a statement: one exception in the text makes it FALSE.","tr":"İfadede \"only\", \"always\", \"never\": metindeki tek bir istisna onu FALSE yapar.","fa":"«only»، «always»، «never» در جمله: یک استثنا در متن آن را FALSE می‌کند."},{"en":"Notes: two numbers or dates sit close together. The heading decides which one you need.","tr":"Notlar: iki sayı ya da tarih yan yanadır. Hangisinin gerektiğine başlık karar verir.","fa":"یادداشت‌ها: دو عدد یا تاریخ نزدیک هم‌اند. عنوان تعیین می‌کند کدام را لازم داری."}],"example":{"text":"The hazel dormouse was once found in woods across most of England. Its range has shrunk by about half since 1900, mainly because the hedges that linked woodlands were removed. Most surviving populations are now in the south.","item":"Statement: The dormouse has always lived only in the south of England.  (TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"\"Once found in woods across most of England\" contradicts \"always... only in the south\".","tr":"\"Bir zamanlar İngiltere’nin çoğunda\" bulunması, \"her zaman... yalnızca güneyde\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"«زمانی در جنگل‌های بیشتر انگلستان بود» با «همیشه... فقط در جنوب» در تضاد است."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-nature"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-nature","n":37,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 37 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 37’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۷ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Sections, people, summary","tr":"Bölümler, kişiler, özet","fa":"بخش‌ها، آدم‌ها، خلاصه"},"body":{"en":"Questions 27-31: which section, A-G, contains each piece of information. Questions 32-36: match each statement to one of five people, A-E. Questions 37-40: complete a summary with ONE WORD ONLY from the passage. Letters may be used more than once.","tr":"Soru 27-31: her bilgi hangi bölümde (A-G). Soru 32-36: her ifadeyi beş kişiden biriyle (A-E) eşleştir. Soru 37-40: bir özeti metinden YALNIZCA BİR KELİMEYLE tamamla. Harfler birden fazla kullanılabilir.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۲۷ تا ۳۱: هر اطلاعات در کدام بخش (A تا G) است. سؤال‌های ۳۲ تا ۳۶: هر جمله را با یکی از پنج نفر (A تا E) جور کن. سؤال‌های ۳۷ تا ۴۰: یک خلاصه را فقط با یک کلمه از متن کامل کن. حرف‌ها را می‌شود بیش از یک بار به کار برد."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Work from easy to hard","tr":"Kolaydan zora çalış","fa":"از آسان به سخت برو"},"steps":[{"en":"Read the summary title and find the part of the passage it covers; do the summary first.","tr":"Özet başlığını oku ve metnin hangi kısmını kapsadığını bul; önce özeti yap.","fa":"عنوان خلاصه را بخوان و بخشی از متن را که پوشش می‌دهد پیدا کن؛ اول خلاصه را حل کن."},{"en":"Mark every name in the passage. For each statement, read what that person says, not what the paragraph says.","tr":"Metindeki her ismi işaretle. Her ifade için paragrafın değil, o kişinin söylediğini oku.","fa":"همه‌ی اسم‌ها را در متن علامت بزن. برای هر جمله، حرف همان شخص را بخوان، نه حرف کل پاراگراف را."},{"en":"For \"which section\", underline the kind of detail asked for: a warning, a reason, a comparison.","tr":"\"Hangi bölüm\" için istenen ayrıntı türünün altını çiz: bir uyarı, bir neden, bir karşılaştırma.","fa":"برای «کدام بخش»، زیر نوع جزئیات خواسته‌شده خط بکش: هشدار، دلیل، مقایسه."},{"en":"Leave the hardest one for last; never spend more than two minutes on one question.","tr":"En zorunu sona bırak; tek bir soruya iki dakikadan fazla harcama.","fa":"سخت‌ترین را برای آخر بگذار؛ هیچ‌وقت بیشتر از دو دقیقه روی یک سؤال نمان."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Same topic, different detail","tr":"Aynı konu, farklı ayrıntı","fa":"همان موضوع، جزئیاتِ دیگر"},"body":{"en":"Several sections talk about cost, risk or success. The question asks for one precise detail, such as \"a comparison of the cost of two animals\". Check that the section contains exactly that, not just the topic.","tr":"Birkaç bölüm maliyet, risk ya da başarıdan söz eder. Soru tek ve kesin bir ayrıntı ister, örneğin \"iki hayvanın maliyet karşılaştırması\". Bölümde yalnızca konunun değil, tam olarak o ayrıntının olduğunu kontrol et.","fa":"چند بخش درباره‌ی هزینه، خطر یا موفقیت حرف می‌زنند. سؤال یک جزئیات دقیق می‌خواهد، مثلاً «مقایسه‌ی هزینه‌ی دو حیوان». مطمئن شو بخش دقیقاً همان را دارد، نه فقط همان موضوع را."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One summary gap, step by step","tr":"Bir özet boşluğu, adım adım","fa":"یک جای خالی خلاصه، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.","text":"\"Young trees are planted in spring. They must be protected from deer, which strip the bark in winter when other food is scarce.\"","item":"Summary: Deer damage young trees in winter because there is little other ___ available.","answer":"food","walk":[{"en":"Find the place: \"deer\" and \"winter\".","tr":"Yeri bul: \"deer\" ve \"winter\".","fa":"جایش را پیدا کن: «deer» و «winter»."},{"en":"\"Little other ___ available\" = \"other food is scarce\".","tr":"\"Little other ___ available\" = \"other food is scarce\".","fa":"«little other ___ available» یعنی «other food is scarce»."},{"en":"Copy one word from the passage: food.","tr":"Metinden tek kelime kopyala: food.","fa":"یک کلمه از متن کپی کن: food."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"\"Some owners think a cat needs milk every day. Actually, most adult cats cannot digest it well,\" says the vet, Dr Moss. Statement: \"A popular belief about feeding cats is mistaken.\" Who says this?","options":["the owners","Dr Moss","nobody"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Dr Moss reports the belief and corrects it with \"actually\".","tr":"Dr Moss inanışı aktarıyor ve \"actually\" ile düzeltiyor.","fa":"دکتر ماس این باور را نقل می‌کند و با «actually» اصلاحش می‌کند."}},"remember":{"en":"Summary first, names marked, and match the exact detail, not the topic.","tr":"Önce özet, isimler işaretli; konuyu değil, tam ayrıntıyı eşleştir.","fa":"اول خلاصه، اسم‌ها علامت‌خورده؛ جزئیات دقیق را جور کن، نه موضوع را."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x08-r3-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-08","unit":"x08-r3"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 3","title":{"en":"The donkey in the field","tr":"Tarladaki eşek","fa":"الاغِ توی مزرعه"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-nature"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.","passage":"The donkey in the field\n\nA  For as long as sheep have been kept, farmers have lost animals to predators. In different parts of the world the threat comes from foxes, coyotes, wolves or simply from dogs that have been allowed to roam. The traditional responses were blunt: predators were shot, trapped or poisoned, and high fences were put up where farmers could afford them. These methods were costly, often only partly effective, and increasingly unpopular with a public that values wildlife. Over the last fifty years, interest has grown in a gentler idea: placing an animal in the field whose job is to protect the flock. Dogs bred for this work are the best known, and llamas have their supporters, but some of the most surprising results have come from an animal more often associated with beach rides than with guard duty, the donkey.\n\nB  Donkeys appear to have a natural dislike of dogs and their wild relatives. Faced with an intruder, a donkey will often bray loudly, put its head down and charge, and it may kick or bite if the animal does not retreat. This behaviour is instinctive, so very little training is needed. Donkeys also have practical advantages. They eat the same grass as the sheep and need no special food, they rarely need a vet, and a healthy animal can work for twenty years or more. For a small farm, the cost of buying and keeping a donkey is a fraction of the cost of a specialist guard dog, which must be fed meat and trained for many months.\n\nC  Evidence for their effectiveness, however, is mixed. Surveys of farmers who use donkeys report fewer losses, sometimes dramatically fewer, but such surveys rely on what farmers remember and are not controlled experiments. Ewan Lockhart, an agricultural adviser who has visited dozens of farms using guard donkeys, describes the results as \"a lottery\". On some farms, he says, losses fell almost to nothing in the first season; on others, apparently similar, nothing changed at all. \"The donkey is not a machine,\" he argues. \"Whether it works depends on the animal, the land and the way it is introduced.\"\n\nD  Researchers have tried to identify the conditions that make success more likely. One finding is consistent: a single donkey works better than two. When two donkeys share a field, they tend to stay together and pay little attention to the sheep. The behavioural scientist Priya Venkataraman stresses the importance of bonding. \"A donkey protects what it regards as its own group,\" she explains. \"If it is put in with strange sheep and left, it may ignore them. It needs to live alongside the flock, ideally for several weeks, before it will treat them as companions worth defending.\" Females and castrated males are generally recommended, since uncastrated males can be aggressive towards lambs. Donkeys also seem most effective in open pasture, where they can see an approaching predator, and in relatively small flocks. Against packs of wolves they offer little protection, and no responsible adviser would suggest otherwise.\n\nE  Keeping a donkey with sheep is not without risks to the donkey itself. Donkeys evolved in dry regions with poor vegetation, and the rich grass of a lowland sheep farm can be too much for them. The veterinary surgeon Carmen Ibarra sees the results regularly. \"Farmers assume that if the grass is good enough for sheep, it must be good for the donkey,\" she says. \"In fact, rich pasture leads to obesity and to a painful disease of the feet. Many guard donkeys are overweight.\" Donkeys also need dry shelter, because their coats, unlike those of sheep, are not waterproof, and their hooves must be trimmed every couple of months. During lambing, some farmers move the donkey out altogether, because a few individuals have been known to injure newborn lambs.\n\nF  Supporters often present guard animals as good for wildlife as well as for farmers. If predators are scared away rather than killed, fewer foxes and coyotes die, and the use of poison, which also kills birds of prey and other species, can be reduced. The wildlife ecologist Jonas Ekdahl has studied farms in areas where guard animals have become common, and he found a clear fall in the number of predators killed by farmers. He adds a note of caution, however. \"A fox that is chased out of one field does not stop eating,\" he points out. \"It goes to the next farm, where the sheep may have no protection at all. If only a few farms use guard animals, the problem may simply move elsewhere.\"\n\nG  Guard donkeys, then, are neither a miracle nor a failure. They are a cheap, low-technology tool that can work well in the right conditions and poorly in the wrong ones. Graham Tully, who keeps around four hundred sheep on hill land and has used donkeys for fifteen years, thinks the mistake many farmers make is to expect too much from a single measure. \"My donkey is one part of the system,\" he says. \"I still check the fences, and I still bring the ewes close to the house at lambing time. The donkey works best when it isn't working alone.\" Researchers would like to test such combinations properly, with careful comparisons between farms, and several studies of this kind are now under way.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 27-31. Reading Passage 3 has seven sections, A-G. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-info","bank":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"questions":[{"n":27,"kind":"match","prompt":"a warning that the animal’s food may damage its health","correct":4,"evidence":"rich pasture leads to obesity and to a painful disease of the feet","why":{"en":"E: Ibarra explains that rich grass makes donkeys fat and causes a foot disease.","tr":"E: Ibarra, zengin otun eşekleri şişmanlattığını ve ayak hastalığına yol açtığını anlatıyor.","fa":"E: ایبارا توضیح می‌دهد که علف پربار الاغ را چاق می‌کند و بیماری پا می‌آورد."},"trap":["TR-detail","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":28,"kind":"match","prompt":"a reason why two guard animals together may be less effective than one","correct":3,"evidence":"they tend to stay together and pay little attention to the sheep","why":{"en":"D: two donkeys \"stay together and pay little attention to the sheep\".","tr":"D: iki eşek \"birlikte kalır ve koyunlara pek ilgi göstermez\".","fa":"D: دو الاغ «کنار هم می‌مانند و به گوسفندها توجه چندانی نمی‌کنند»."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":29,"kind":"match","prompt":"a reference to the ways farmers dealt with predators in the past","correct":0,"evidence":"predators were shot, trapped or poisoned","why":{"en":"A: \"the traditional responses\": shooting, trapping, poison and fences.","tr":"A: \"geleneksel tepkiler\": vurmak, tuzak, zehir ve çitler.","fa":"A: «واکنش‌های سنتی»: شلیک، تله، سم و حصار."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":30,"kind":"match","prompt":"a comparison of the cost of two kinds of guard animal","correct":1,"evidence":"a fraction of the cost of a specialist guard dog","why":{"en":"B: a donkey costs \"a fraction of\" a guard dog. The cost of fences in A is not a comparison between animals.","tr":"B: bir eşek, bekçi köpeğinin maliyetinin \"küçük bir kısmı\". A’daki çit maliyeti hayvanlar arasında bir karşılaştırma değil.","fa":"B: الاغ «کسری از» هزینه‌ی سگ نگهبان را دارد. هزینه‌ی حصار در A مقایسه‌ای بین حیوان‌ها نیست."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]},{"n":31,"kind":"match","prompt":"a suggestion that the problem may be moved rather than solved","correct":5,"evidence":"the problem may simply move elsewhere","why":{"en":"F: a fox chased from one field \"goes to the next farm\".","tr":"F: bir tarladan kovulan tilki \"bir sonraki çiftliğe gider\".","fa":"F: روباهی که از یک مزرعه رانده می‌شود «به مزرعه‌ی بعدی می‌رود»."},"trap":["TR-detail"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 32-36. Look at the following statements (Questions 32-36) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A, B, C, D or E. Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 32-36 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-features","bank":["A Ewan Lockhart","B Priya Venkataraman","C Jonas Ekdahl","D Carmen Ibarra","E Graham Tully"],"questions":[{"n":32,"kind":"match","prompt":"It is difficult to predict whether a guard donkey will be successful.","correct":0,"evidence":"describes the results as","why":{"en":"Lockhart calls the results \"a lottery\": similar farms, different results.","tr":"Lockhart sonuçlara \"piyango\" diyor: benzer çiftlikler, farklı sonuçlar.","fa":"لاکهارت نتیجه‌ها را «بخت‌آزمایی» می‌نامد: مزرعه‌های شبیه، نتیجه‌های متفاوت."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":33,"kind":"match","prompt":"A donkey needs time with the sheep before it will defend them.","correct":1,"evidence":"It needs to live alongside the flock","why":{"en":"Venkataraman: it must live with the flock \"for several weeks\" first.","tr":"Venkataraman: önce sürüyle \"birkaç hafta\" yaşamalı.","fa":"ونکاتارامان: اول باید «چند هفته» کنار گله زندگی کند."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]},{"n":34,"kind":"match","prompt":"Many farmers wrongly believe that grass suitable for sheep is also suitable for donkeys.","correct":3,"evidence":"if the grass is good enough for sheep, it must be good for the donkey","why":{"en":"Ibarra: \"Farmers assume...\" and then \"In fact, rich pasture leads to obesity\".","tr":"Ibarra: \"Çiftçiler sanıyor ki...\" ve ardından \"Aslında zengin mera şişmanlığa yol açar\".","fa":"ایبارا: «کشاورزها خیال می‌کنند...» و بعد «در واقع مرتع پربار به چاقی منجر می‌شود»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":35,"kind":"match","prompt":"Fewer wild animals are killed in areas where guard animals are used.","correct":2,"evidence":"a clear fall in the number of predators killed by farmers","why":{"en":"Ekdahl found \"a clear fall in the number of predators killed\".","tr":"Ekdahl \"öldürülen yırtıcı sayısında açık bir düşüş\" buldu.","fa":"اکدال «کاهشی روشن در تعداد شکارچی‌های کشته‌شده» پیدا کرد."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]},{"n":36,"kind":"match","prompt":"A guard donkey should be one of several methods used together.","correct":4,"evidence":"The donkey works best when it isn't working alone","why":{"en":"Tully still checks fences and moves ewes at lambing: the donkey is \"one part of the system\".","tr":"Tully hâlâ çitleri kontrol ediyor ve kuzulamada koyunları yaklaştırıyor: eşek \"sistemin bir parçası\".","fa":"تالی هنوز حصارها را چک می‌کند و موقع زایمان میش‌ها را نزدیک خانه می‌آورد: الاغ «بخشی از سیستم» است."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 37-40. Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"summary","summaryTitle":"Choosing and placing a guard donkey","questions":[{"n":37,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The donkey should live with the flock for some weeks so that it sees the sheep as ___.","accept":["companions"],"limit":1,"evidence":"treat them as companions worth defending","why":{"en":"\"Treat them as companions worth defending\". Keep the plural.","tr":"\"Onları korumaya değer arkadaşlar olarak görür\". Çoğulu koru.","fa":"«آن‌ها را همراهانی می‌داند که ارزش دفاع دارند». جمع را نگه دار."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":38,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Uncastrated males are not recommended, because they may be ___ towards lambs.","accept":["aggressive"],"limit":1,"evidence":"uncastrated males can be aggressive towards lambs","why":{"en":"\"Can be aggressive towards lambs\".","tr":"\"Kuzulara karşı saldırgan olabilir\".","fa":"«ممکن است نسبت به بره‌ها پرخاشگر باشند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":39,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Donkeys are most useful in open ___, where they can see predators coming.","accept":["pasture"],"limit":1,"evidence":"most effective in open pasture","why":{"en":"\"Most effective in open pasture, where they can see an approaching predator\".","tr":"\"Bir yırtıcının yaklaştığını görebildikleri açık merada en etkili\".","fa":"«در مرتع باز بیشترین اثر را دارند، جایی که شکارچیِ در حال نزدیک شدن را می‌بینند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":40,"kind":"gap","prompt":"They give little protection against ___ of wolves.","accept":["packs"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Against packs of wolves they offer little protection","why":{"en":"\"Against packs of wolves they offer little protection\". Plural.","tr":"\"Kurt sürülerine karşı az koruma sağlarlar\". Çoğul.","fa":"«در برابر گله‌های گرگ محافظت کمی می‌کنند». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural","TR-limit"]}]}],"id":"c-x08-r3-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-08","unit":"x08-r3"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"The behaviour is instinctive.\" This means the animal...","options":["does it naturally, without being taught","learns it from people","does it only when it is hungry"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Instinctive = natural, not learned.","tr":"Instinctive = doğal, öğrenilmemiş.","fa":"instinctive یعنی غریزی، یادنگرفته."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":3,"prompt":"A statement says \"results are hard to predict\". Which phrase in a passage matches it?","options":["it is a fraction of the cost","it is instinctive","it is a lottery"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"A lottery = you cannot know the result in advance.","tr":"Piyango = sonucu önceden bilemezsin.","fa":"بخت‌آزمایی یعنی نتیجه را از قبل نمی‌دانی."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Which question set is usually best to start with in this passage?","options":["the sections, because they cover the whole passage","the summary, because it covers one part of the passage","the people, because there are five"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"The summary is tied to one part of the text, so it is quick to locate.","tr":"Özet metnin bir kısmına bağlıdır, bu yüzden yerini bulmak hızlıdır.","fa":"خلاصه به یک بخش از متن مربوط است، پس پیدا کردنش سریع است."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Question: \"Which section mentions a comparison between the costs of two methods?\" Section A says fences are \"costly\". Section C compares the price of nets and traps. Answer?","options":["C","A","both"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"A mentions cost, but only C compares two methods.","tr":"A maliyetten söz ediyor ama yalnızca C iki yöntemi karşılaştırıyor.","fa":"A از هزینه حرف می‌زند، اما فقط C دو روش را مقایسه می‌کند."}}],"id":"c-x08-r3-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-08","unit":"x08-r3"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 3: a long article","tr":"GT Reading Section 3: uzun bir makale","fa":"GT Reading Section 3: یک مقاله‌ی بلند"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to choose a heading for each paragraph of a long article, complete a summary with one word from the text, and answer multiple choice questions.","tr":"Bu derste uzun bir makalenin her paragrafına bir başlık seçmeyi, bir özeti metinden tek kelimeyle tamamlamayı ve çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری برای هر پاراگراف یک مقاله‌ی بلند عنوان انتخاب کنی، یک خلاصه را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی و به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای جواب بدهی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Paragraphs","tr":"Paragraf","fa":"پاراگراف"},"value":"A-F"},{"label":{"en":"Headings","tr":"Başlık","fa":"عنوان"},"value":"i-viii"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: a village under a reservoir","tr":"Bu sınav: baraj gölünün altında bir köy","fa":"این آزمون: روستایی زیر مخزن آب"},"intro":{"en":"GT Section 3 is one long article on a general topic. History and heritage are among the most frequent subjects, often told as the story of one place.","tr":"GT Section 3 genel bir konuda tek bir uzun makaledir. Tarih ve miras en sık çıkan konulardandır; çoğu zaman tek bir yerin hikâyesi olarak anlatılır.","fa":"GT Section 3 یک مقاله‌ی بلند درباره‌ی موضوعی عمومی است. تاریخ و میراث از پرتکرارترین موضوع‌هایند و اغلب به شکل داستان یک مکان روایت می‌شوند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x08-r3gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT3-history","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"GT3-history","n":14,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 14 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 14’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۴ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A local history: a village lost to a reservoir","tr":"Yerel bir tarih: baraj gölüne kurban giden bir köy","fa":"تاریخی محلی: روستایی که زیر مخزن آب رفت"},"asks":{"en":"A general-interest article tells the story of a place in six paragraphs: what can be seen today, why it changed, how people reacted, what happened to them, what was saved and how it is remembered. You choose a heading for each paragraph, complete a summary and answer multiple choice questions.","tr":"Genel ilgi çeken bir makale bir yerin hikâyesini altı paragrafta anlatıyor: bugün ne görülebildiği, neden değiştiği, insanların nasıl tepki verdiği, onlara ne olduğu, neyin kurtarıldığı ve nasıl hatırlandığı. Her paragrafa bir başlık seçiyor, bir özeti tamamlıyor ve çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplıyorsun.","fa":"یک مقاله‌ی عمومی داستان یک مکان را در شش پاراگراف تعریف می‌کند: امروز چه چیزی دیده می‌شود، چرا تغییر کرد، مردم چه واکنشی نشان دادند، چه بر سرشان آمد، چه چیزی نجات داده شد و چطور به یاد آورده می‌شود. برای هر پاراگراف عنوان انتخاب می‌کنی، یک خلاصه را کامل می‌کنی و به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای جواب می‌دهی."},"fields":["Today","The reason for the change","The reaction","The move","What was saved","How it is remembered"],"words":[{"a":"reappear","b":"begin to appear again / come back into view","tr":"yeniden ortaya çıkmak","fa":"دوباره پیدا شدن"},{"a":"site","b":"a place chosen for something","tr":"alan, yer","fa":"محل"},{"a":"opposition","b":"protests / a petition / meetings against","tr":"muhalefet, karşı çıkma","fa":"مخالفت"},{"a":"delay","b":"hold up / slow down","tr":"geciktirmek","fa":"به تأخیر انداختن"},{"a":"compensation","b":"money for what was lost","tr":"tazminat","fa":"غرامت"},{"a":"painful","b":"hard / sad / upsetting","tr":"acı verici","fa":"دردناک"},{"a":"record","b":"photograph / measure / draw","tr":"kaydetmek, belgelemek","fa":"ثبت کردن"},{"a":"remains","b":"what is left of a building","tr":"kalıntılar","fa":"بقایا"},{"a":"keep the memory alive","b":"make sure people do not forget","tr":"anısını yaşatmak","fa":"یاد را زنده نگه داشتن"},{"a":"archive","b":"a collection of records","tr":"arşiv","fa":"آرشیو"},{"a":"under pressure","b":"running short / not enough","tr":"baskı altında","fa":"تحت فشار"}],"traps":[{"en":"A heading can repeat a word from the paragraph and still be wrong: paragraph B mentions the dam, but it is about why the valley was chosen.","tr":"Bir başlık paragraftaki bir kelimeyi tekrar edip yine de yanlış olabilir: B paragrafı barajdan söz ediyor ama konusu vadinin neden seçildiği.","fa":"یک عنوان ممکن است کلمه‌ای از پاراگراف را تکرار کند و باز هم غلط باشد: پاراگراف B از سد حرف می‌زند، اما موضوعش دلیل انتخاب دره است."},{"en":"The last sentence of a paragraph may add a side detail. Choose the heading for the main idea of the whole paragraph.","tr":"Bir paragrafın son cümlesi yan bir ayrıntı ekleyebilir. Başlığı bütün paragrafın ana fikrine göre seç.","fa":"جمله‌ی آخر پاراگراف ممکن است یک جزئیات فرعی اضافه کند. عنوان را بر اساس ایده‌ی اصلی کل پاراگراف انتخاب کن."}],"example":{"text":"\"The town grew rapidly after the railway arrived in 1860. New streets were laid out, and the population doubled in twenty years. A small museum now tells this story.\"","item":"Best heading: A A museum for the town  B Growth brought by the railway","answer":"B","why":{"en":"The museum is a final detail; the paragraph is about growth after the railway.","tr":"Müze son bir ayrıntı; paragraf demiryolundan sonraki büyüme hakkında.","fa":"موزه یک جزئیات پایانی است؛ پاراگراف درباره‌ی رشد بعد از آمدن راه‌آهن است."}}},{"id":"GT3-history","ctx":["GT3-history"],"title":{"en":"History and heritage","tr":"Tarih ve kültürel miras","fa":"تاریخ و میراث"},"asks":{"en":"A longer text about a historical topic: a road, a bridge, a trade, a craft, an invention or a job that has disappeared. Headings follow the story; summaries and multiple choice test causes and changes.","tr":"Tarihî bir konu hakkında daha uzun bir metin: bir yol, bir köprü, bir ticaret, bir zanaat, bir icat ya da ortadan kalkmış bir meslek. Başlıklar hikâyeyi izler; özetler ve çoktan seçmeli sorular nedenleri ve değişimleri sınar.","fa":"متنی بلندتر درباره‌ی یک موضوع تاریخی: یک جاده، یک پل، یک تجارت، یک صنعت دستی، یک اختراع یا شغلی که از بین رفته. عنوان‌ها داستان را دنبال می‌کنند؛ خلاصه‌ها و سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای علت‌ها و تغییرها را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["The arrival of the railway","A dangerous job","Why the trade came to an end","How the material was collected","Life for the workers’ families"],"words":[{"a":"era","b":"period / age","tr":"dönem","fa":"دوره"},{"a":"originally","b":"at first / in the beginning","tr":"başlangıçta","fa":"در اصل"},{"a":"workers","b":"labourers / crew","tr":"işçiler","fa":"کارگران"},{"a":"dangerous","b":"risky / hazardous","tr":"tehlikeli","fa":"خطرناک"},{"a":"decline","b":"fall-off / became less common","tr":"gerileme","fa":"افول"},{"a":"take over from","b":"replace","tr":"... -in yerini almak","fa":"جای ... را گرفتن"},{"a":"skills","b":"expertise / know-how","tr":"beceriler","fa":"مهارت‌ها"},{"a":"preserved","b":"kept / still exists","tr":"korunmuş","fa":"حفظ‌شده"},{"a":"remote","b":"far from towns / isolated","tr":"ıssız, uzak","fa":"دورافتاده"},{"a":"demand","b":"what people wanted to buy","tr":"talep","fa":"تقاضا"},{"a":"eventually","b":"in the end / finally","tr":"sonunda","fa":"سرانجام"},{"a":"transport","b":"carry goods / move","tr":"taşımak","fa":"حمل کردن"}],"traps":[{"en":"Headings in time order: two paragraphs may describe the same period from different angles.","tr":"Kronolojik başlıklar: iki paragraf aynı dönemi farklı açılardan anlatabilir.","fa":"عنوان‌های زمانی: دو پاراگراف ممکن است یک دوره را از دو زاویه توصیف کنند."},{"en":"Summary gaps: the word must also fit the grammar of the summary sentence.","tr":"Özet boşlukları: kelime özet cümlesinin dilbilgisine de uymalı.","fa":"جاهای خالی خلاصه: کلمه باید با دستور جمله‌ی خلاصه هم جور باشد."}],"example":{"text":"C  By the 1950s, lorries could carry goods faster and more cheaply than boats. Traffic on the canal fell year by year, and the last regular cargo boat stopped running in 1963.","item":"Choose the heading for paragraph C:  i  Losing out to road transport   ii  How the canal was dug   iii  A dangerous journey","answer":"i","why":{"en":"Lorries were faster and cheaper, so canal traffic fell: losing out to road transport.","tr":"Kamyonlar daha hızlı ve ucuzdu; kanal trafiği azaldı: karayoluna yenilmek.","fa":"کامیون‌ها سریع‌تر و ارزان‌تر بودند، پس رفت‌وآمد کانال کم شد: باختن به حمل‌ونقل جاده‌ای."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT3-history"],"often":{"pattern":"GT3-history","n":14,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 14 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 14’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۴ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Headings, summary, choices","tr":"Başlıklar, özet, seçimler","fa":"عنوان‌ها، خلاصه، گزینه‌ها"},"body":{"en":"Questions 28-33: choose the right heading, i-viii, for paragraphs A-F; two headings are not used. Questions 34-37: complete a summary with ONE WORD ONLY from the text. Questions 38-40: choose A, B, C or D.","tr":"Soru 28-33: A-F paragrafları için doğru başlığı (i-viii) seç; iki başlık kullanılmaz. Soru 34-37: bir özeti metinden YALNIZCA BİR KELİMEYLE tamamla. Soru 38-40: A, B, C ya da D’yi seç.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۲۸ تا ۳۳: برای پاراگراف‌های A تا F عنوان درست (i تا viii) را انتخاب کن؛ دو عنوان استفاده نمی‌شوند. سؤال‌های ۳۴ تا ۳۷: خلاصه را فقط با یک کلمه از متن کامل کن. سؤال‌های ۳۸ تا ۴۰: A، B، C یا D را انتخاب کن."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Headings in four steps","tr":"Dört adımda başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌ها در چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Read all eight headings first and note the key idea of each.","tr":"Önce sekiz başlığın hepsini oku ve her birinin ana fikrini not et.","fa":"اول هر هشت عنوان را بخوان و ایده‌ی کلیدی هرکدام را یادداشت کن."},{"en":"Read one paragraph and say its main idea in five words.","tr":"Bir paragraf oku ve ana fikrini beş kelimeyle söyle.","fa":"یک پاراگراف بخوان و ایده‌ی اصلی‌اش را در پنج کلمه بگو."},{"en":"Choose the heading that covers the whole paragraph, not one sentence.","tr":"Tek bir cümleyi değil, bütün paragrafı kapsayan başlığı seç.","fa":"عنوانی را انتخاب کن که کل پاراگراف را پوشش بدهد، نه یک جمله را."},{"en":"Cross out headings as you use them, and come back to any paragraph you are unsure about.","tr":"Kullandıkça başlıkların üstünü çiz ve emin olmadığın paragrafa sonra dön.","fa":"عنوان‌ها را وقتی استفاده کردی خط بزن و به پاراگرافی که مطمئن نیستی بعداً برگرد."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"A shared word is not the main idea","tr":"Ortak kelime ana fikir değil","fa":"کلمه‌ی مشترک ایده‌ی اصلی نیست"},"body":{"en":"Wrong headings often borrow a word from the paragraph: \"dam\", \"farmers\", \"museum\". Ask what the paragraph is mainly about, then check the heading says that.","tr":"Yanlış başlıklar çoğu zaman paragraftan bir kelime ödünç alır: \"dam\", \"farmers\", \"museum\". Paragrafın esas olarak ne hakkında olduğunu sor, sonra başlığın bunu söyleyip söylemediğine bak.","fa":"عنوان‌های غلط اغلب کلمه‌ای از پاراگراف قرض می‌گیرند: «dam»، «farmers»، «museum». بپرس پاراگراف اصولاً درباره‌ی چیست و بعد ببین عنوان همین را می‌گوید یا نه."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One heading, step by step","tr":"Bir başlık, adım adım","fa":"یک عنوان، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Choose the correct heading for the paragraph.","text":"\"When the factory closed in 1985, two thousand people lost their jobs. Shops on the high street emptied, and many young families moved away to find work. A local newspaper called it the year the town stopped.\"","item":"Headings: i A newspaper’s view  ii The effects of a closure  iii New jobs for young families","answer":"ii","walk":[{"en":"Main idea in five words: the factory closing hurt the town.","tr":"Beş kelimeyle ana fikir: fabrikanın kapanması kasabaya zarar verdi.","fa":"ایده‌ی اصلی در پنج کلمه: بسته شدن کارخانه به شهر آسیب زد."},{"en":"i is only the last sentence; iii is the opposite of what happened.","tr":"i yalnızca son cümle; iii olanın tam tersi.","fa":"i فقط جمله‌ی آخر است؛ iii برعکسِ چیزی است که اتفاق افتاد."},{"en":"ii covers jobs, shops and families: the effects of the closure.","tr":"ii işleri, dükkânları ve aileleri kapsıyor: kapanmanın etkileri.","fa":"ii شغل‌ها، مغازه‌ها و خانواده‌ها را پوشش می‌دهد: اثرهای تعطیلی."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"A paragraph describes a festival’s history, its music and its food, and ends: \"Tickets sell out quickly.\" Which heading fits best?","options":["How to buy tickets","A new festival","What the festival offers"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Tickets are only the last detail; the paragraph is about what the festival offers.","tr":"Biletler yalnızca son ayrıntı; paragraf festivalin sunduklarıyla ilgili.","fa":"بلیت فقط جزئیات آخر است؛ پاراگراف درباره‌ی چیزهایی است که جشنواره ارائه می‌دهد."}},"remember":{"en":"A heading names the main idea of the whole paragraph; ignore headings that only repeat a word.","tr":"Başlık bütün paragrafın ana fikrini söyler; yalnızca bir kelimeyi tekrarlayan başlıklara aldanma.","fa":"عنوان ایده‌ی اصلی کل پاراگراف را می‌گوید؛ فریب عنوان‌هایی را که فقط یک کلمه را تکرار می‌کنند نخور."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x08-r3-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-08","unit":"x08-r3"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 3","title":{"en":"The village beneath the water","tr":"Suyun altındaki köy","fa":"روستای زیر آب"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT3-history"],"texts":[{"title":"The village beneath the water","kind":"article","body":"A  In a long, dry summer, something strange happens at Thornmere reservoir. As the water level falls, the tops of stone walls begin to appear, followed by the outline of a lane, the arch of a small bridge and finally the base of a church tower. For a few weeks, people come from all over the region to walk among the ruins of a village that disappeared under the water more than seventy years ago. Local cafés stay open late, and the car parks along the shore are full every weekend. Then the autumn rain arrives, and Thornmere is hidden once again.\n\nB  The story of the village begins with the needs of a city forty kilometres away. In the 1930s, its factories and growing population were using far more water than local rivers could supply, and engineers began to search the surrounding hills for a site for a reservoir. The Thorn valley had everything they wanted. It received some of the highest rainfall in the county, and at its southern end the valley narrowed into a rocky gorge where a dam could be built at a reasonable cost. The fact that around three hundred people lived in the valley was, for the engineers, a secondary concern. Their reports from the time discuss rock types, rainfall figures and the cost of pipes in great detail, but mention the village itself in only a few lines.\n\nC  The residents saw it differently. Most families had farmed in the valley for generations, and many had never lived anywhere else. When the plans were announced, the village held public meetings, and a petition signed by almost every adult was sent to Parliament. Letters in the local newspaper described the scheme as the theft of a community. The protests delayed the work by several years, but they could not stop it. In the end, the city's need for water was judged to be more important, and every household was offered compensation for its land and buildings.\n\nD  Rather than leave the families to scatter, the water authority agreed to build a new village on the hillside above the reservoir. The houses there were small but modern, and for many residents they brought comforts they had never had before, such as electricity and indoor bathrooms. The authority also built a school, a shop and a village hall, and it tried to keep neighbours next to each other, so that people who had lived side by side in the valley would do so again on the hill. Even so, older people in particular found the move painful. The new village had no history, and for years many of them walked down to the water's edge on Sundays to look at the place where their homes had been. The graves in the old churchyard were moved, with great care, to a new cemetery beside the new church.\n\nE  Before the valley was flooded, a small team of historians and archaeologists was given just eighteen months to record what was about to be lost. They photographed every building, measured the church and made drawings of carved stones. Their most important discovery was the remains of a medieval mill beside the river, which showed that people had been grinding grain in the valley for at least six hundred years. Some objects, including the church bell and a carved doorway, were removed and taken to the county museum, where they can still be seen today. The rest was left where it stood, and most of the houses were pulled down to the height of their ground floors before the water arrived.\n\nF  Today, few people who lived in the old village are still alive, but their children and grandchildren have worked hard to keep its memory alive. A local history group has recorded interviews with former residents, describing everything from harvest festivals to the day the water began to rise. These recordings, together with the team's photographs, have been made into an online archive that schools in the area use in their history lessons. When the ruins reappear, the group also runs guided walks, though it worries about visitors climbing on the fragile walls. For the water company, the reappearance of the village is a less welcome sight: it is a clear sign that the region's water supply is under pressure. Each time the walls appear, the company repeats its request for households to use less water, and local newspapers print photographs of the ruins beside the warnings. In this way, a village that was drowned to provide water has become a reminder of how valuable that water is."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 28-33. The text has six paragraphs, A-F. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. Write the correct number, i-viii, in boxes 28-33 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"headings","bank":["i A new source of income for farmers","ii Why this valley was chosen","iii Recording the past before it was lost","iv The technical problems of building the dam","v A sight that returns in dry weather","vi Keeping the memory of the village alive","vii Opposition from the people of the valley","viii A new home on higher ground"],"questions":[{"n":28,"kind":"match","prompt":"Paragraph A","correct":4,"evidence":"the tops of stone walls begin to appear","why":{"en":"A describes the ruins that appear when the water falls in a dry summer.","tr":"A, kurak bir yazda su çekilince ortaya çıkan kalıntıları anlatıyor.","fa":"A ویرانه‌هایی را توصیف می‌کند که وقتی در تابستان خشک آب پایین می‌رود ظاهر می‌شوند."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":29,"kind":"match","prompt":"Paragraph B","correct":1,"evidence":"The Thorn valley had everything they wanted","why":{"en":"B: high rainfall and a narrow gorge for the dam = why the valley was chosen. The dam is mentioned, but no technical problems.","tr":"B: yüksek yağış ve baraj için dar bir boğaz = vadinin neden seçildiği. Barajdan söz ediliyor ama teknik sorunlardan değil.","fa":"B: باران زیاد و تنگه‌ای باریک برای سد یعنی دلیل انتخاب دره. از سد حرف زده شده، اما نه از مشکلات فنی."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]},{"n":30,"kind":"match","prompt":"Paragraph C","correct":6,"evidence":"a petition signed by almost every adult was sent to Parliament","why":{"en":"C: meetings, a petition and letters against the scheme = opposition.","tr":"C: toplantılar, bir dilekçe ve plana karşı mektuplar = muhalefet.","fa":"C: جلسه‌ها، طومار و نامه‌هایی علیه طرح یعنی مخالفت."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":31,"kind":"match","prompt":"Paragraph D","correct":7,"evidence":"build a new village on the hillside above the reservoir","why":{"en":"D: the new village on the hillside = a new home on higher ground.","tr":"D: yamaçtaki yeni köy = daha yüksekte yeni bir yuva.","fa":"D: روستای جدید روی دامنه یعنی خانه‌ای تازه در جای بلندتر."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":32,"kind":"match","prompt":"Paragraph E","correct":2,"evidence":"given just eighteen months to record what was about to be lost","why":{"en":"E: photographs, measurements and the mill discovery before the flooding.","tr":"E: sel basmadan önce fotoğraflar, ölçümler ve değirmenin bulunması.","fa":"E: عکس‌ها، اندازه‌گیری‌ها و کشف آسیاب پیش از آب‌گرفتگی."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":33,"kind":"match","prompt":"Paragraph F","correct":5,"evidence":"have worked hard to keep its memory alive","why":{"en":"F: interviews, an online archive and guided walks. The water company’s concern is a detail, not the main idea.","tr":"F: röportajlar, bir çevrimiçi arşiv ve rehberli yürüyüşler. Su şirketinin kaygısı bir ayrıntı, ana fikir değil.","fa":"F: مصاحبه‌ها، آرشیو آنلاین و پیاده‌روی با راهنما. نگرانی شرکت آب یک جزئیات است، نه ایده‌ی اصلی."},"trap":["TR-detail"]}]},{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 34-37. Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","qtype":"summary","summaryTitle":"Leaving the valley","questions":[{"n":34,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Each household was given ___ for the land and buildings it lost.","accept":["compensation"],"limit":1,"evidence":"every household was offered compensation","why":{"en":"\"Every household was offered compensation for its land and buildings.\"","tr":"\"Her haneye arazisi ve binaları için tazminat teklif edildi.\"","fa":"«به هر خانوار برای زمین و ساختمان‌هایش غرامت پیشنهاد شد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":35,"kind":"gap","prompt":"A new village was built on the ___ above the reservoir.","accept":["hillside"],"limit":1,"evidence":"build a new village on the hillside above the reservoir","why":{"en":"\"On the hillside above the reservoir\". One word.","tr":"\"Baraj gölünün yukarısındaki yamaçta\". Tek kelime.","fa":"«روی دامنه‌ی بالای مخزن». یک کلمه."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":36,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The ___ in the old churchyard were moved to a new cemetery.","accept":["graves"],"limit":1,"evidence":"The graves in the old churchyard were moved","why":{"en":"\"The graves in the old churchyard were moved.\" Plural, because of \"were\".","tr":"\"Eski kilise bahçesindeki mezarlar taşındı.\" \"were\" yüzünden çoğul.","fa":"«قبرهای حیاط کلیسای قدیمی منتقل شدند». به‌خاطر «were» جمع است."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":37,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Before the flooding, the remains of a medieval ___ were found beside the river.","accept":["mill"],"limit":1,"evidence":"the remains of a medieval mill beside the river","why":{"en":"\"The remains of a medieval mill beside the river\".","tr":"\"Nehrin kenarında ortaçağdan kalma bir değirmenin kalıntıları\".","fa":"«بقایای یک آسیاب قرون وسطایی کنار رودخانه»."},"trap":["TR-limit"]}]},{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 38-40. Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","qtype":"mcq","questions":[{"n":38,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Why do people visit Thornmere reservoir in some summers?","options":["A to swim in the shallow water","B to explore the remains of the old village","C to take part in a festival","D to watch repairs to the dam"],"correct":1,"evidence":"people come from all over the region to walk among the ruins","why":{"en":"They come \"to walk among the ruins of a village that disappeared under the water\".","tr":"\"Suyun altında kaybolan bir köyün kalıntıları arasında yürümek için\" geliyorlar.","fa":"می‌آیند تا «میان ویرانه‌های روستایی که زیر آب رفته قدم بزنند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":39,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What does the writer say about the engineers’ reports from the 1930s?","options":["A They exaggerated the cost of the dam.","B They were kept secret from the villagers.","C They suggested a different valley.","D They paid little attention to the village."],"correct":3,"evidence":"mention the village itself in only a few lines","why":{"en":"Rock, rainfall and pipes in detail, but the village \"in only a few lines\".","tr":"Kaya, yağış ve borular ayrıntılı, ama köy \"yalnızca birkaç satırda\".","fa":"سنگ، باران و لوله‌ها با جزئیات، اما روستا «فقط در چند خط»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":40,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What is the online archive used for?","options":["A teaching history in local schools","B selling photographs of the ruins","C organising guided walks","D raising money for the county museum"],"correct":0,"evidence":"schools in the area use in their history lessons","why":{"en":"\"Schools in the area use [it] in their history lessons.\" The walks are run by the group, not through the archive.","tr":"\"Bölgedeki okullar tarih derslerinde kullanıyor.\" Yürüyüşleri grup düzenliyor, arşiv değil.","fa":"«مدرسه‌های منطقه در درس تاریخ از آن استفاده می‌کنند». پیاده‌روی‌ها را گروه برگزار می‌کند، نه آرشیو."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-samewords"]}]}],"id":"c-x08-r3-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-08","unit":"x08-r3"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Every household was offered compensation.\" Compensation is...","options":["a new job","money paid for a loss","a written apology"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Compensation = money given because you lost something.","tr":"Compensation = bir kaybın karşılığında verilen para.","fa":"compensation یعنی پولی که به‌خاطر چیزی که از دست داده‌ای می‌دهند."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"Which heading means the same as \"Opposition from the people of the valley\"?","options":["Residents fight the plan","The valley’s population grows","People welcome the change"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Opposition = fighting or protesting against something.","tr":"Opposition = bir şeye karşı mücadele ya da protesto.","fa":"opposition یعنی مخالفت و اعتراض به چیزی."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"You have six paragraphs and eight headings. What should you do with a heading you have used?","options":["Use it again for the next paragraph","Ignore the instructions","Cross it out unless the instructions allow reuse"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Each heading is normally used once; crossing it out makes the rest easier.","tr":"Her başlık normalde bir kez kullanılır; üstünü çizmek kalanları kolaylaştırır.","fa":"هر عنوان معمولاً یک بار به کار می‌رود؛ خط زدنش بقیه را آسان‌تر می‌کند."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"A paragraph explains how a bridge was designed and ends: \"The engineer later moved to Canada.\" Which heading fits?","options":["An engineer’s new life abroad","Designing the bridge","Problems with the bridge"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"The move to Canada is a final detail; the paragraph is about the design.","tr":"Kanada’ya taşınma son bir ayrıntı; paragraf tasarımla ilgili.","fa":"رفتن به کانادا جزئیات آخر است؛ پاراگراف درباره‌ی طراحی است."}}],"id":"c-x08-r3-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-08","unit":"x08-r3"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
